# The RAUC this project builds, and the source it is built from.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. Debian's rauc is built with -Dstreaming=true, which links
# libcurl-gnutls and drags GnuTLS, p11-kit, GMP, Nettle and the Kerberos
# libraries into a signed appliance image. Measured on the x64 image: /usr/bin/
# rauc was the ONLY consumer of libcurl-gnutls in the whole root, and mos does
# not use streaming at all -- os/update/rauc/manifest.raucm.in records the adaptive/
# streaming install path as DEFERRED, so what is actually shipped is an
# operator running `rauc install` on a local file.
#
# A second TLS stack in an image whose own daemons use rustls on purpose is not
# a size problem, it is a patching-surface problem. Built here with network and
# streaming off, rauc links libc, libcrypto, libfdisk, glib and json-glib --
# every one of which the image already carries for other reasons.
#
# THE VERSION BECOMES A DECISION IN THIS REPOSITORY, the same way
# os/podman/versions.env makes the container engine's version one. It is pinned
# to the release Debian 13 also ships, so that moving off the distribution
# package changes exactly one thing at a time: how rauc is built, not which
# rauc runs. Bumping is this file's job.
#
# HOW TO BUMP: change the tag, set the hash to the literal string PENDING, and
# run `make os-rauc`. The build prints the hash it computed and fails; paste it
# in and run again. Recording a hash is then an act rather than a copy from a
# page nobody re-checked.
#
# THE PARENTHESIS THAT USED TO STAND HERE — "(under MOS_RAUC_STRICT=1)" — WENT
# WITH THE KNOB IN RFCT-108 M2c. Unlike os/podman/versions.env, whose prose
# claimed a failure the code did not perform, this file named the condition
# honestly; what it did not say is that the condition was never met. Nothing in
# this repository set MOS_RAUC_STRICT=1: not the workflows, not the Makefile,
# not os/update/rauc/build.sh, which passed `${MOS_RAUC_STRICT:-0}` through. A
# value that is never 1 makes the parenthesis the only place the behaviour
# exists, so the default is now the behaviour and there is no knob.
RAUC_VERSION=v1.13
RAUC_SHA256=372828c23a52f73cb0e4f55e0ed6eca4563bbc8c0e557392ff8a888973087941
